course: dictionary
lesson: 1734
title: One word, three meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. You can find the right one by reading the words around it. The word clam is a good example. «The walrus uses its tusks to haul itself onto the ice, and finds clams with its whiskers.» Here a clam is a sea animal that lives buried in sand or mud.
explain: Now read this: «The chef served clam chowder, a thick soup, with warm bread.» Here clam means food. Chowder is a soup you eat, so the clam is seafood. Always ask: which meaning fits this sentence? Then put your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
explain: Clam can also be a verb, an action word. «When the teacher asked why he was late, Sam clammed up and said nothing.» To clam up means to suddenly stop talking, often because you are nervous or do not want to tell. The words said nothing are the clue.
fact: A clam is an animal with a soft body inside two hard shells joined by a hinge.
fact: Clams live buried in sand or mud, in the sea or in rivers.
fact: Clams are molluscs, like snails and mussels, and they filter tiny food from the water.
fact: «The giant clam is the biggest clam in the world.» It can be bigger than a child.
fact: «Clam up» means to suddenly stop talking. «Happy as a clam» (US) means very happy.
exercise: «The walrus finds clams with its whiskers.» What is a clam in this sentence? | A hard rock on the beach | A type of seal | *A sea animal with a soft body inside two hard shells | A long tusk
exercise: «The chef served clam chowder with warm bread.» What is a clam in this sentence? | A tall tree | An animal that lives on land | A hinge on a box | *Seafood, eaten as food
exercise: «When the teacher asked, Sam clammed up and said nothing.» What does clammed up mean? | *Suddenly stopped talking | Went to sleep | Shouted very loudly | Ran out of the room
test: «The giant clam can be bigger than a child.» What does this tell you? | *Some clams can be very large | Clams are always small | Clams live in trees | Clams can talk
test: Mia says, «She is happy as a clam.» What does she mean? | She is sleepy | She is very hungry | She is cold and wet | *She is very happy
exam: «A clam from Iceland named Ming lived about five hundred and seven years.» What does this show? | Clams can only live for one day | Clams have no shells | Clams cannot live in the sea | *Some clams live for hundreds of years
